  "body": [
    { "line_index": 0, "verse": "149:2", "verse_number_printed": "2", "verse_marker": "†", "text": "† Let Iſrael be ioyful in him, that made him: and let the" },
    { "line_index": 1, "verse": "149:2", "text": "children of Sion reioyce in their king." },
    { "line_index": 2, "verse": "149:3", "verse_number_printed": "3", "verse_marker": "†", "text": "† Let them praiſe his name in quire: on tymbrel, and pſalter" },
    { "line_index": 3, "verse": "149:3", "text": "let them ſing to him:" },
    { "line_index": 4, "verse": "149:4", "verse_number_printed": "4", "verse_marker": "†", "text": "† Becauſe our Lord is wel pleaſed in his people: and he wil" },
    { "line_index": 5, "verse": "149:4", "text": "exalt the meeke vnto ſaluation." },
    { "line_index": 6, "verse": "149:5", "verse_number_printed": "5", "verse_marker": "†", "text": "† The ſainctes ſhal reioyce in glorie: they ſhal be ioyful" },
    { "line_index": 7, "verse": "149:5", "text": "in their beddes.", "ref_letters_present": ["b"] },
    { "line_index": 8, "verse": "149:6", "verse_number_printed": "6", "verse_marker": "†", "text": "† The exaltations of God in their throte: and two edged", "ref_letters_present": ["c", "d"] },
    { "line_index": 9, "verse": "149:6", "text": "ſwordes in their handes." },
    { "line_index": 10, "verse": "149:7", "verse_number_printed": "7", "verse_marker": "†", "text": "† To doe reuenge in the nations: chaſtiſements among the" },
    { "line_index": 11, "verse": "149:7", "text": "peoples." },
    { "line_index": 12, "verse": "149:8", "verse_number_printed": "8", "verse_marker": "†", "text": "† To binde their kinges in fetters: and their nobles in yron" },
    { "line_index": 13, "verse": "149:8", "text": "manicles." },
    { "line_index": 14, "verse": "149:9", "verse_number_printed": "9", "verse_marker": "†", "text": "† That they may doe in them the iudgement that is written:", "ref_letters_present": ["e"] },
    { "line_index": 15, "verse": "149:9", "text": "this glorie is to al his ſainctes. Alleluia.", "ref_letters_present": ["f"] },
    { "line_index": 16, "verse": "150:1", "verse_number_printed": "1", "text": "Alleluia.", "note": "Ps150 opening rubric line before the drop-cap" },
    { "line_index": 17, "verse": "150:1", "dropcap": "P", "text": "PRAYSE ye our Lord in his holies: prayſe ye him in", "ref_letters_present": ["a"] },
    { "line_index": 18, "verse": "150:1", "text": "the firmament of his ſtrength.", "ref_letters_present": ["b"] },
    { "line_index": 19, "verse": "150:2", "verse_number_printed": "2", "verse_marker": "†", "text": "† Prayſe ye him in his powers: prayſe ye him according", "ref_letters_present": ["c", "d"] },
    { "line_index": 20, "verse": "150:2", "text": "to the multitude of his greatnes." }
  ],
  "apparatus": [
    { "role": "argument", "anchor_verse": "150:1", "text": "God abſolutly moſt excellent is to be praiſed, 3. with al ſortes of inſtruments, and by al other meanes.", "marginal_gloss": "God moſt excellent and moſt laudable. the firſt key." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "c", "anchor_verse": "149:6", "face": "vv-for-w", "text": "Hiegheſt praiſes of God ſhal be continually vttered by Sainctes in glorie: for ſtil as praiſes paſſe by their tongues and mouthes, more like praiſes ſhal ſuccede from their throte, and hartie affection, ſo out of the abundance of the hart their mouth ſhal ſtil ſpeake Gods praiſe." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "d", "anchor_verse": "149:6", "face": "vv-for-w", "text": "Glorified Sainctes ſhal alſo haue iudiciarie povvre. First, al in general ſhal like and approue Gods iuſtice in puniſhing the vvicked. Secondly the vvicked ſhal be iuſtly condemned in compariſon of the bleſſed, vvho paſſed through, and ouercame the like, yea and greater tribulations and tentations then thoſe, by vvhich the damned vvere ouercome. Thirdly, certaine more excellent Sainctes, namely the Apoſtles, and al thoſe that forſaking proprietie of temporal goodes, geue that they haue to the poore, as ſome religious Orders doe; or into a Communitie as the Apoſtles, and manie primitiue Chriſtians did (Mat. 4. v. 20. cap. 19. v. 27. Act. 4. v. 34. 1. Cor. 6. v. 3.) ſhal ſitte in iudgement ſeates, aſſeſſorie iudges with Chriſt, and iudge thoſe that render account, of wel or euil ſpending the temporal landes or goodes, which they poſſeſſed in this vvorld. So teach S. Auguſtin S. Ierom, S. Beda, and others." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "b", "anchor_verse": "149:5", "text": "eternal reſt." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "e", "anchor_verse": "149:9", "text": "Decreed by God." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "f", "anchor_verse": "149:9", "face": "vv-for-w", "text": "This iudicial povvre is part of Sainctes glorie." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "a", "anchor_verse": "150:1", "text": "Al ye Angels and men that are in the holie and higheſt heauen praiſe our Lord." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "b", "anchor_verse": "150:1", "text": "Al ye creatures that are in, and vnder the firſt moueable firmament praiſe our Lord." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "c", "anchor_verse": "150:2", "face": "w-uncertain", "text": "And you eſpecially (Gods peculiar people) amongſt whom, and for whom, diuine miracles haue bene wrought praiſe our Lord, with al your poſſible endeuoure, for though his infinite Excellencie excedeth the powre of al creatures to praiſe him ſufficiently, yet it reſteth that you may infinitly extend your wil and deſire to praiſe our Lord, according to the multitude of his greatnes." },
    { "role": "annotation_marginal_right", "anchor_verse": "149:2", "text": "are bond to praiſe, only accepteth thoſe mens praiſes, that liue in his holie Church." }
  ],
  "marginalia": [
